{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"GHSA-v6rj-xm57-3p59","published":"2026-11-12T23:41:50Z","modified":"2026-11-12T23:45:03.296036447Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-126078"],"summary":"Action View: Possible XSS vulnerability in highlight helper","details":"### Impact\n`ActionView::Helpers::TextHelper#highlight` substitutes each matched phrase into the `:highlighter` string without escaping it and returns the result marked HTML-safe. Because sanitizing leaves quote characters in text unescaped, a match substituted into a quoted attribute value of the highlighter, such as the `<a href=\"search?q=\\1\">` form shown in the method's documentation, could end the attribute value and add attributes to the element, possibly leading to XSS. Applications are affected when they pass a `:highlighter` that places a placeholder inside an attribute value and highlight text or phrases that a user controls. The default `<mark>\\1</mark>` highlighter and the block form are not affected.\n\n### Details\nThe fixed releases HTML-escape each group substituted into the `:highlighter` string, so quotes in a match are rendered as `&quot;` and `&#39;`. Only the numbered placeholders `\\0` to `\\9` are expanded; other `String#sub` replacement escapes, such as `\\k<name>`, `\\&` and `\\\\`, are left as written. A match can no longer begin on the `>` that closes a preceding tag. Escaping makes a placeholder safe as element content or inside a quoted attribute value, but not in an unquoted attribute value, a URL, JavaScript or CSS context, or an attribute whose value is HTML. See the Action View CHANGELOG for details.\n\n### Workarounds\nUse a `:highlighter` that places the matched phrase only in element content, such as the default `<mark>\\1</mark>`.\n\n### Releases\nThe fixed releases are available at the normal locations.\n\nPatches for those who cannot upgrade at once:\n- 8.1: https://github.com/rails/rails/commit/06938194b4fd59e1d2c8ab4a781f3c1e2b763425.patch\n- 8.0: https://github.com/rails/rails/commit/c796f6198837479ada13290eb8fa767b5219a58a.patch\n\n### Credit\nThis issue was found by the Anthropic OSS Scanner (ANT-2026-THHUJQVO).","affected":[{"package":{"name":"actionview","ecosystem":"RubyGems","purl":"pkg:gem/actionview"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"8.1.0.beta1"},{"fixed":"8.1.4.1"}]}],"versions":["8.1.0","8.1.0.beta1","8.1.0.rc1","8.1.1","8.1.2","8.1.2.1","8.1.3","8.1.3.1","8.1.4"],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/11/GHSA-v6rj-xm57-3p59/GHSA-v6rj-xm57-3p59.json"}},{"package":{"name":"actionview","ecosystem":"RubyGems","purl":"pkg:gem/actionview"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.0.5.2"}]}],"versions":["4.1.0","4.1.0.beta1","4.1.0.beta2","4.1.0.rc1","4.1.0.rc2","4.1.1","4.1.10","4.1.10.rc1","4.1.10.rc2","4.1.10.rc3","4.1.10.rc4","4.1.11","4.1.12","4.1.12.rc1","4.1.13","4.1.13.rc1","4.1.14","4.1.14.1","4.1.14.2","4.1.14.rc1","4.1.14.rc2","4.1.15","4.1.15.rc1","4.1.16","4.1.16.rc1","4.1.2","4.1.2.rc1","4.1.2.rc2","4.1.2.rc3","4.1.3","4.1.4","4.1.5","4.1.6","4.1.6.rc1","4.1.6.rc2","4.1.7","4.1.7.1","4.1.8","4.1.9","4.1.9.rc1","4.2.0","4.2.0.beta1","4.2.0.beta2","4.2.0.beta3","4.2.0.beta4","4.2.0.rc1","4.2.0.rc2","4.2.0.rc3","4.2.1","4.2.1.rc1","4.2.1.rc2","4.2.1.rc3","4.2.1.rc4","4.2.10","4.2.10.rc1","4.2.11","4.2.11.1","4.2.11.2","4.2.11.3","4.2.2","4.2.3","4.2.3.rc1","4.2.4","4.2.4.rc1","4.2.5","4.2.5.1","4.2.5.2","4.2.5.rc1","4.2.5.rc2","4.2.6","4.2.6.rc1","4.2.7","4.2.7.1","4.2.7.rc1","4.2.8","4.2.8.rc1","4.2.9","4.2.9.rc1","4.2.9.rc2","5.0.0","5.0.0.1","5.0.0.beta1","5.0.0.beta1.1","5.0.0.beta2","5.0.0.beta3","5.0.0.beta4","5.0.0.racecar1","5.0.0.rc1","5.0.0.rc2","5.0.1","5.0.1.rc1","5.0.1.rc2","5.0.2","5.0.2.rc1","5.0.3","5.0.4","5.0.4.rc1","5.0.5","5.0.5.rc1","5.0.5.rc2","5.0.6","5.0.6.rc1","5.0.7","5.0.7.1","5.0.7.2","5.1.0","5.1.0.beta1","5.1.0.rc1","5.1.0.rc2","5.1.1","5.1.2","5.1.2.rc1","5.1.3","5.1.3